{"name":"Nathlekh","status":"ok","title":"Nathlekh","pageId":18927,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Nathlekh</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p116-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"aliases\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Aliases</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">City of Cats</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">City</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Shining_Plains\" title=\"Shining Plains\">Shining Plains</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Vilhon_Reach\" title=\"Vilhon Reach\">Vilhon Reach</a><br/><small><b>Formerly:</b></small> <a href=\"/wiki/Nathlan\" title=\"Nathlan\">Nathlan</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_Coast\" title=\"Dragon Coast\">Dragon Coast</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Large city</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Humans\" title=\"Humans\">Humans</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/Shou\" title=\"Shou\">Shou</a>),<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p116-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> <a href=\"/wiki/Werecat\" title=\"Werecat\">werecats</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Werelion\" title=\"Werelion\">werelions</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Weretiger\" title=\"Weretiger\">weretigers</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-P&amp;P-p42-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Nobanion\" title=\"Nobanion\">Nobanion</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRHoF-90_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRHoF-90-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sharess\" title=\"Sharess\">Sharess</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-P&amp;P-p42-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Politics<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p116-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-P&amp;P-p42-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"government\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a class=\"extiw\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feudal\" title=\"wikipedia:Feudal\">Feudal</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"executive\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Executive</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Council_of_the_Cat_Lords\" title=\"Council of the Cat Lords\">Council of the Cat Lords</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">18,000<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p116-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> in <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6SW5oYWJpdGFudHNfb2ZfTmF0aGxla2g/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Nathlekh (page does not exist)\">Inhabitants of  Nathlekh</span></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Nathlekh\" title=\"Category:Locations in Nathlekh\">Locations in  Nathlekh</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Nathlekh\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Nathlekh\">Organizations in  Nathlekh</a></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Nathlekh</b>, called the <b>City of Cats</b>, was a city on the <a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_Coast\" title=\"Dragon Coast\">Dragon Coast</a> and the capital of the <a href=\"/wiki/Shou\" title=\"Shou\">Shou</a> nation of <a href=\"/wiki/Nathlan\" title=\"Nathlan\">Nathlan</a> in the late 15<sup>th</sup> century <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/DR\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p116-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> By <a href=\"/wiki/1501_DR\" title=\"1501 DR\">early 16<sup>th</sup> century DR</a>, The city was classified as a settlement of the <a href=\"/wiki/Shining_Plains\" title=\"Shining Plains\">Shining Plains</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/Vilhon_Reach\" title=\"Vilhon Reach\">Vilhon Reach</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRHoF-90_3-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRHoF-90-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Law_&amp;_Order\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Law &amp; Order</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Foreign_Quarter\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Foreign Quarter</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inhabitants</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Notable_Individuals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Individuals</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Located at the western edge of the <a href=\"/wiki/Gulthmere_Forest\" title=\"Gulthmere Forest\">Gulthmere Forest</a> on the shores of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Lake_of_the_Long_Arm\" title=\"Lake of the Long Arm\">Lake of the Long Arm</a>, Nathlekh was built around a <a href=\"/wiki/Granite\" title=\"Granite\">granite</a> plug, atop which the <a href=\"/wiki/Pride_of_Nobanion_(building)\" title=\"Pride of Nobanion (building)\">Pride of Nobanion</a> stood, seemingly as an extension of the rock.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-P&amp;P-p42-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It was originally populated by feline <a href=\"/wiki/Lycanthrope\" title=\"Lycanthrope\">lycanthropes</a> worshiping <a href=\"/wiki/Nobanion\" title=\"Nobanion\">Nobanion</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Sharess\" title=\"Sharess\">Sharess</a>. It had a significant population of mundane <a href=\"/wiki/Cat\" title=\"Cat\">cats</a> (including <a href=\"/wiki/Lion\" title=\"Lion\">lions</a>) and its mysterious rulers were known as the Cat Lords.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-P&amp;P-p42-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> All of these factors certainly earned it its moniker.\n</p><p>In the <a href=\"/wiki/1386_DR\" title=\"1386 DR\">Year of the Halflings' Lament, 1386 DR</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Spellplague\" title=\"Spellplague\">Spellplague</a> caused the ground underneath the Shou ward of the city to rise several hundred feet higher then the rest of the city. This destroyed much of the non-Shou parts of the city.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-p103_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-p103-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In the <a href=\"/wiki/1394_DR\" title=\"1394 DR\">Year of Deaths Unmourned, 1394 DR</a>, the city outlawed refugees and <a href=\"/wiki/Fey\" title=\"Fey\">fey</a> from entering the city.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-p107_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-p107-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Settled by more and more immigrants from <a href=\"/wiki/Kara-Tur\" title=\"Kara-Tur\">Kara-Tur</a> over the centuries, by <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479 DR</a>, the city had become populated almost entirely by Shou and the small nation of Nathlan had grown up around it. The citizens of Nathlekh were suspicious of outsiders. They forbade anyone not of Shou descent (especially non-<a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">humans</a>) from taking up residence in the city and restricted visitors to a single, special section of the city. By this time, the city had largely ceased to be called the \"City of Cats\".<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p116-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/1501_DR\" title=\"1501 DR\">Year of the Shining Mythal, 1501 DR</a>, the independent city-state was abounded by cats as a local sight and worshipped Nobanion.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FRHoF-90_3-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRHoF-90-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Law_.26_Order\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Law_&amp;_Order\">Law &amp; Order</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Law &amp; Order\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Law &amp; Order\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Under the Cat Lords in the 1300s DR, a trio of <a href=\"/wiki/Lammasu\" title=\"Lammasu\">lammasu</a> judges passed judgement once a week on lawbreakers.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-P&amp;P-p42-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dt>Sky District</dt>\n<dd>This was the name given to the Shou ward of the city that rested on the high ground.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-p104_6-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-p104-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> During the events of the Spellplague, a slow but inexorable earth movement thrust a majority of the district several hundred feet higher than the rest of the city. Hundreds of structures along the edges of the fault were destroyed.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-ch.9_7-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-ch.9-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>The Dragon Bridge</dt>\n<dd>A wide and thick stone bridge that went from the ground near the piers on Long Arm Lake and rose in a diagonal line up to the Sky District. The bridge was so named for its supporting arches, each of which took the form of a sculpted, sinuous stone dragon. Each successively larger stone dragon statue bore the weight of its span differently. A series of three massive, gated checkpoints guarded the bridge.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-p104_6-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-p104-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>City of the Dead</dt>\n<dd>The so-called \"city of the dead\" was the graveyard district, where the deceased were interred. The area was decorated with countless <a href=\"/wiki/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a> markers and 4‑foot-high (1.2‑meter), hardened clay structures resembling beehives.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-ch.9_7-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-ch.9-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The granite entry arch adorned the entrance into the graveyard.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-p110_8-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-p110-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Foreign_Quarter\">Foreign Quarter</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Foreign Quarter\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Foreign Quarter\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dt>The Bear Pit</dt>\n<dd>A western-style warehouse that hid an underground gambling den and fighting arena where bets were placed on captured <a href=\"/wiki/Dog\" title=\"Dog\">dogs</a> and other animals. The <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV2hpdGVfUGV0YWxfdG9uZz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"White Petal tong (page does not exist)\">White Petal tong</span>, who ran the establishment, occasionally had people who crossed them fight the animals. The building backed onto a confusing maze of alleyways.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Chiang Emporium</dt>\n<dd>The main base of a Shou trading coster that operated along the <a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_Coast\" title=\"Dragon Coast\">Dragon Coast</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_of_Fallen_Stars\" title=\"Sea of Fallen Stars\">Sea of Fallen Stars</a>. It was owned and operated by the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2hpYW5nX0NsYW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Chiang Clan (page does not exist)\">Chiang Clan</span>, a powerful family that seemed to consist entirely of women.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-6_10-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-6-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-7_11-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-7-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG2-1_12-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG2-1-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Flying Tiger Inn</dt>\n<dd>On the outside, this inn appeared to have been built in the western style but inside, it was decorated exclusively in Shou style. It was owned and operated by Master <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV29vP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Woo (page does not exist)\">Woo</span>, a small bald man with a very long white mustache.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Four Winds tea house</dt>\n<dd>A traditional Shou <a href=\"/wiki/Tea_house\" title=\"Tea house\">tea house</a> owned by the influential <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTmVuZ19DbGFuP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Neng Clan (page does not exist)\">Neng Clan</span>. Propriety was important here and those who offended Shou social norms were asked to leave.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Ho Fan Dye Works</dt>\n<dd>This old factory on East Street, located at the edge of the industrial area in the Foreign Quarter, was an old building that acted as the White Petal tong's headquarters. The tong's elderly Grandmaster <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVHN1aV9TaG9rdT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Tsui Shoku (page does not exist)\">Tsui Shoku</span> lived here, well-protected by guards, traps and other defenses.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>House of Flowers</dt>\n<dd>The local temple of <a href=\"/wiki/Kelemvor\" title=\"Kelemvor\">Kelemvor</a>. Although not a Shou god, this temple was where the annual <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTmlnaHRfb2ZfRmFsbGVuX1BldGFscz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Night of Fallen Petals (page does not exist)\">Night of Fallen Petals</span> occurred in the city.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-6_10-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-6-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Ironhand's Forge</dt>\n<dd>A high-quality smithy run by the <a href=\"/wiki/Shield_dwarf\" title=\"Shield dwarf\">shield dwarf</a> <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRWxtdW5kX0lyb25oYW5kP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Elmund Ironhand (page does not exist)\">Elmund Ironhand</span>, who opened his business in <a href=\"/wiki/1469_DR\" title=\"1469 DR\">1469 DR</a> and enjoyed the company of the Shou despite their haughtiness and pride.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Lo-Yun's butcher's shop</dt>\n<dd>This otherwise average-looking and smelly butcher's shop stood atop a soundproofed dojo operated by the White Petal tong. Lo-Yun's pigs were quite accustomed to being fed human meat.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-4_13-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-4-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Mak Won Emporium</dt>\n<dd>Next door to the Flying Tiger, this shop sold everything an alchemist could ever need. The owner was an elderly Shou man named <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvWXVfTWFrX1dvbj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Yu Mak Won (page does not exist)\">Yu Mak Won</span>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Mensyn's Wares</dt>\n<dd>A cobbler's and leatherworking shop owned by the eccentric and incredibly rich <a href=\"/wiki/Halfling\" title=\"Halfling\">halfling</a> <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSm9uc3Rlcl9ZYXRlP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Jonster Yate (page does not exist)\">Jonster Yate</span>, one of the Seven Burghers of <a href=\"/wiki/New_Velar\" title=\"New Velar\">New Velar</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-6_10-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-6-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Snow Blossom gambling house</dt>\n<dd>A traditional Shou building laquered in red, green, and gold with a sleeping stone dragon reclining on the roof. This popular gambling den was operated by <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGFrX01laT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Tak Mei (page does not exist)\">Tak Mei</span> as a front for the White Petal tong but its games were rigged and run by expert cheats and con men. The criminals used debts accrued by the patrons to blackmail them.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-6_10-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-6-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Temple of Tymora</dt>\n<dd>A beautiful building run by a priest named <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTWFya2xlP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Markle (page does not exist)\">Markle</span>. Brother Berak (originally from <a href=\"/wiki/Westgate\" title=\"Westgate\">Westgate</a>) and a Shou man known as Brother <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTXU/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Mu (page does not exist)\">Mu</span>, helped Markle.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-5_9-7\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvWWlfQW1haGw/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Yi Amahl (page does not exist)\">Yi Amahl</span>'s shop</dt>\n<dd>A prophet from <a href=\"/wiki/Almraiven\" title=\"Almraiven\">Almraiven</a> sold <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Coffee\" title=\"Coffee\">coffee</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Calishite\" title=\"Calishite\">Calishite</a> trinkets here with his apprentice <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUGV0ZWM/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Petec (page does not exist)\">Petec</span>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DRAG1-6_10-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DRAG1-6-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inhabitants\">Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Individuals\">Notable Individuals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Individuals\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Individuals\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQWlseW5fS2FuZT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Ailyn Kane (page does not exist)\">Ailyn Kane</span>, a <a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">human</a> toddler adopted by the <a href=\"/wiki/Monk\" title=\"Monk\">monk</a> Raidon Kane in the late 14<sup>th</sup> century <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/DR\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>..<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-ch.1_14-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-ch.1-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> She was killed by fallen debris during the start of the <a href=\"/wiki/Spellplague\" title=\"Spellplague\">Spellplague</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/1385_DR\" title=\"1385 DR\">1385 DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-ch.9_7-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-ch.9-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Raidon_Kane\" title=\"Raidon Kane\">Raidon Kane</a>, a <a href=\"/wiki/Shou\" title=\"Shou\">Shou</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Half-elf\" title=\"Half-elf\">half</a>–<a href=\"/wiki/Star_elf\" title=\"Star elf\">star elf</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Monk\" title=\"Monk\">monk</a> and a <a href=\"/wiki/Keepers_of_the_Cerulean_Sign\" title=\"Keepers of the Cerulean Sign\">Keeper of the Cerulean Sign</a> who moved to the city from <a href=\"/wiki/Telflamm\" title=\"Telflamm\">Telflamm</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/1381_DR\" title=\"1381 DR\">1381 DR</a> to have a better life for his daughter Ailyn, but his home was destroyed with the onset of the Spellplague. He did not have the chance to return to his ruined house until <a href=\"/wiki/1396_DR\" title=\"1396 DR\">1396 DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-ch.1_14-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-ch.1-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PoS-ch.9_7-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PoS-ch.9-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Nathlekh?veaction=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRCG-p116-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-2\">1.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-3\">1.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-4\">1.4</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCG-p116_1-5\">1.5</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Bruce_R._Cordell\" title=\"Bruce R. Cordell\">Bruce R. Cordell</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Chris_Sims\" title=\"Chris Sims\">Chris Sims</a> (August 2008). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide\">Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide</a></i>. Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/Jennifer_Clarke_Wilkes\" title=\"Jennifer Clarke Wilkes\">Jennifer Clarke Wilkes</a>, <i>et al</i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p. 116. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-4924-3\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-4924-3\">978-0-7869-4924-3</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-P&amp;P-p42-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-1\">2.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-2\">2.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-3\">2.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-4\">2.4</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-P&amp;P-p42_2-5\">2.5</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eric_L._Boyd\" title=\"Eric L. Boyd\">Eric L. Boyd</a> (September 1997). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Powers_%26_Pantheons\" title=\"Powers &amp; Pantheons\">Powers &amp; Pantheons</a></i>. Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/Julia_Martin\" title=\"Julia Martin\">Julia Martin</a>. (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 42. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0786906574\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0786906574\">978-0786906574</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRHoF-90-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRHoF-90_3-0\">3.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRHoF-90_3-1\">3.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRHoF-90_3-2\">3.2</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a> (November 2025). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms:_Heroes_of_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Forgotten Realms: Heroes of Faerûn\">Forgotten Realms: Heroes of Faerûn</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p. 90. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-6580-9\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-6580-9\">978-0-7869-6580-9</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-PoS-p103-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-PoS-p103_4-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Bruce_R._Cordell\" title=\"Bruce R. Cordell\">Bruce R. Cordell</a> (December 2008). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Plague_of_Spells\" title=\"Plague of Spells\">Plague of Spells</a> (Mass Market Paperback)</i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), chap. 9, p. 103. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-4965-6\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-4965-6\">978-0-7869-4965-6</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-PoS-p107-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-PoS-p107_5-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Bruce_R._Cordell\" title=\"Bruce R. Cordell\">Bruce R. Cordell</a> (December 2008). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Plague_of_Spells\" title=\"Plague of Spells\">Plague of Spells</a> (Mass Market Paperback)</i>. (<a